# Endless Story · runner env reference
#
# ⚠️ The runner is a LIBRARY, not a standalone service. Its code runs inside:
#   • the web app's `POST /api/tick` route (the live autonomous loop), and
#   • its own eval/harness scripts, which load `../web/.env.local`
#     (see package.json: `--env-file-if-exists=../web/.env.local`).
# So the runner has NO separate process env — it inherits whichever process runs it.
#
# CANONICAL source of truth = packages/web/.env.example. Put real values in
# ../web/.env.local (or your web deployment's env). This file only documents the
# variables the runner's OWN code paths exercise, so you know which ones affect
# runner behavior (chapter prose, portraits, dreams, memory, on-chain anchoring).

# ── Network (read directly in runner/src) ──
SUI_NETWORK=testnet

# ── Walrus persistence (via @endless-story/memwal · chapters, portraits, dreams, reflections) ──
# With ASSET_SERVICE_URL set, runner-generated blobs publish through your funded asset
# service → the on-chain Blob object is owned by your wallet AND lands in the renewal
# registry (auto-renew). UNSET → falls back to the public testnet publisher: not owned,
# not in the registry, NOT renewable. Set both for any real run.
ASSET_SERVICE_URL=https://assets.zeabur.app
ASSET_SERVICE_SECRET=
# WALRUS_PUBLISHER_URL=                          # explicit publisher override; wins over the asset service
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALRUS_AGGREGATOR=https://walrus.231labs.xyz   # blob read URL written into content

# ── MemWal · SEAL-encrypted character memory (via @endless-story/memwal) ──
# Unset = narrative still runs, just without long-term memory recall/remember.
MEMWAL_PRIVATE_KEY=
MEMWAL_ACCOUNT_ID=0x...
MEMWAL_SERVER_URL=https://memwal-relayer.zeabur.app

# ── LLM · chapter prose + portrait / dream images (via @endless-story/llm) ──
ZAI_API_KEY=
POE_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
AI_PROVIDER=auto                                 # auto | zai | poe | anthropic
